{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/673934-making-a-legendary-first-age-dragonblood","id":673934,"title":"Making a Legendary First Age Dragonblood","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-22T01:20:58-07:00","id":673934,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Making a Legendary First Age Dragonblood","content":"So I'm playing in a First Age game and am wanting to make a Wood Aspected Dragonblood. Thing is, I've only ever played Solaroids. <br /> <br /> <br /> Any tips, advise, must-have charms, etc, that can be advised?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3052-blackshade10","name":"blackshade10","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T01:24:09-07:00","id":673960,"title":"","content":"First and most important question is - What's the concept?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T01:34:49-07:00","id":673963,"title":"","content":"&quot;Cheerful Carouser Under the Star of Destiny&quot;.<br /> <br /> The character is going to be dragged into the upcoming Usurpation, though more because they are destined too, rather than out of an intense desire to do so. Life was more their oyster, enjoying it, even skills like Martial Arts more of a hobby.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3052-blackshade10","name":"blackshade10","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T01:36:29-07:00","id":673964,"title":"","content":"Questions:<br /> First, what sort of help do you want? Crunch, fluff, just spitballing?<br /> Second, what edition of Exalted are you playing?<br /> Third, What is the rest of the party rolling with?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T01:46:05-07:00","id":673968,"title":"","content":"MOSTLY Crunch, I'm really just not familiar with their mechanics. I'm fairly familiar with the fluff in general, though I wouldn't say I know the DB's inside and out.<br /> <br /> Edition is 2.5!<br /> <br /> <br /> Right now, the only confirmed party member is a nutty Ghostblood experiment done by a Solar. I'm the first to really start getting my character ready(that I'm aware of, at least). The party IS limited to Dragonblooded, MAYBE one Siddy(ST was wary and capped at most 1), the Ghostblood, and nothing else.<br /> <br /> The game is starting 6-12 months before the Usurpation, and we're going to be right in the middle of the event.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm open to something other than a Wood, Wood just seemed most appropriate for that type of concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3052,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3052-blackshade10","user":"blackshade10","date":". 09-22-2015, 05:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3052-blackshade10","name":"blackshade10","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T03:12:29-07:00","id":674006,"title":"","content":"Wood seems good for the concept, though Fire also works, as they favour Presence and Socialise.<br /> <br /> I'd say Wood, but take Socialise as favoured: it has some charms for carousing, like a charm that makes all the alcohol at a party really good.<br /> There's some fun charms in Performance (which is Wood) you could use as well. Maybe Medicine... for making sure everyone recovers from the party!<br /> <br /> But honestly, he sounds like maybe a bit of a dilettante, doing various hobbies because he's just having a good time. So I don't really know what you want to take.<br /> <br /> You mentioned martial arts: there's a Wood-aspected style called Orgiastic Fugitive style, for drunken master fighting. I find it a little mechanically complicated though. You need to have a good handle on the poison rules.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T03:24:45-07:00","id":674015,"title":"","content":"Crunch-wise, I would lean heavily on the high-tech nature of the Age of Nightmares for survival. You CAN have something like Celestial Battle Armor, so go for it. If necessary, justify it as yet another indulgence. You will be thankful for it when the long knives come out.<br /> <br /> Another portion of the character sheet that is easy to overlook is Backgrounds. You want to have good friends for the end of the world. The kind of people that are likely to live, and have a vested interest in you living. I'd set myself up with enough status in the Deliberative that I had a position safely ensconced in the Bureaucracy. The goal would be high enough up to not do much work, and low enough down that you wouldn't be working directly with any crazed Solars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T03:54:33-07:00","id":674032,"title":"","content":"Legendary Breeding. You'll want the motes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T07:18:49-07:00","id":674154,"title":"","content":"Charm recommendations. Pick and choose which abilities you like. <br /> <br /> A note on Excellencies: always get the First. For combat abilities, also get the Second and Speciality Focus. Only get Terrestrial Reinforcement if it is a prerequisite or you want your DB to lead mortal groups in this ability (Medicine, Craft, Bureaucracy as well as most combat abilities). Surging Mastery is <i>only </i>good to combo with Extra Action Charms.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Archery:</b></i><br /> <i>Primarily useful for group range defence, it also has one of the few DB unblockable/undodgeable attacks in the form of a counter plus a decent Extra Action.</i><br /> Dragon Graced Arrow (Wood, Water, Fire, Earth)<br /> Dragonfly Finds Mate<br /> Seven Year Swarm Volley<br /> Sparrow Dives at Hawk<br /> Swallows Defend the Nest<br /> <br /> <i><b>Athletics:</b><br /> Mostly unremarkable. Bellows Pumping Stride can be extended to allies. For a larger investment you could have a flying archer but this is easier done with artifacts in the First Age.</i><br /> Effortlessly Rising Flame<br /> Falling Star Maneuver<br /> Bellows Pumping Stride<br /> <br /> <b><i>Awareness:</i></b><br /> <i>A grab bag of scene-long surprise negation, scrying and shaping/crippling attacks. </i><br /> All-Encompassing Earth Sense<br /> Sense Riding Technique<br /> Sense Destroying Method<br /> Essence Disruption Attack<br /> <br /> <b><i>Bureaucracy:</i></b><br /> <i>Home to some of the most potent DB influence Charms, if you want to make a deal, a DB bureaucrat has you covered.</i><br /> Finding the Water's Depths<br /> Thoughtful Gift Technique<br /> Distraction of the Babbling Brook<br /> Drowning in Negotiation Style<br /> <br /> <i><b>Craft:</b></i><br /> <i>Great for quick-building mundane objects and structures, can also boost others in attacking structures.</i><br /> Shaping Hand Style<br /> Stone Carving Fingers Form (Wood, Earth, Fire)<br /> Flaw-Finding Examination<br /> <br /> <i><b>Dodge:</b><br /> DB dodge is pretty solid, with penalty negators, cap-breaking external penalty defences, group defences and counterattacks. The PD is not the best, but worth getting anyway.</i><br /> Threshold Warding Stance<br /> Hopping Firecracker Evasion<br /> Virtuous Negation Defence<br /> Safety Among Enemies<br /> Elemental Defence Technique (Wood, Air)<br /> Smoldering Karma Strike <br /> Unassailable Body of (Element) Defence (Wood, Fire)<br /> <br /> <b><i>Integrity:</i></b><br /> <i>A must have in a Celestial game. Shaping defence, perfect social block and cheap maxed DV and MDV for the scene while in the presence of Celestials.</i><br /> Inviolate Dragon Spirit<br /> Chaos Warding Prana<br /> Defence from Anathema Method<br /> Oath of Ten Thousand Dragons<br /> Undaunted Dragon Hero<br /> <br /> <i><b>Investigation:</b><br /> One of the weaker trees. The E5 capstone Dredged Murmurs Hunch is potentially great, but probably best reserved for PCs.</i><br /> Scent of Crime Method<br /> Falsehood Unearthing Attitude<br /> Revelation of Associates Hunch<br /> Tampering Detection Technique<br /> Bloodhound's Nose Technique<br /> <br /> <i><b>Larceny:</b></i><br /> <i>Like the sister-tree Investigation, it's fairly weak. Unlike Investigation, its E5 capstone is amazing and will likely be helpful for a group.</i><br /> Observer Awareness Method<br /> Ears of the Snowy Owl<br /> Naked Thief Style<br /> Window-In-The-Door Technique<br /> Flowing God-Dragon Stance<br /> <br /> <i><b>Linguistics:</b><br /> Another must-have. Linguistics is divided into language Charms that aren't very useful and communication Charms which definitely are.</i><br /> Wind-Carried Words Technique<br /> Voices on the Wind<br /> Poisoned Tongue Technique<br /> Voice of Mastery<br /> With One Mind<br /> <br /> <i><b>Lore:</b><br /> A grab bag of elemental and mind-expanding powers. At E5, Elemental Bolt Technique is the most accurate attack DBs have. Get The Wind Turns only if your DB has children.</i><br /> Elemental Concentration Trance<br /> Elemental Empowerment Meditation<br /> Glorious Birthright Font<br /> The Wind Turns <br /> Elemental Bolt Attack<br /> Elemental Burst Technique<br /> <br /> <b><i>Martial Arts:</i></b><br /> <i>Not touching this one. What styles are permissible depends heavily on your storyteller. By default Terrestrial Hero is not worth it.</i><br /> <br /> <b><i>Medicine:</i></b><br /> <i>If you lack a Solar physician, a DB is the next best thing.</i><br /> Infection Banishing Prana<br /> Venom Expulsion Method<br /> Madness Analysing Stare<br /> Disease Banishing Technique<br /> Wound Closing Touch<br /> Purity of Mind Method<br /> Most Beneficent Seed of the Five Dragons <br /> Grievous Wound Alternation Energy<br /> Jade Crucible Method x2<br /> <br /> <i><b>Melee:</b><br /> Alone, DB Melee is not bad. Its main strength is to enhance others. With other Melee fighters, it is great. Alongside Solar Melee, it produces monsters.</i><br /> Dragon Graced Weapon (x5)<br /> Refining the Inner Blade<br /> Dragon Blade Beneficence<br /> Portentous Comet-Deflecting Mode<br /> Conflagration of Warding<br /> Threshing Floor Technique<br /> Ringing Anvil Onslaught<br /> <br /> <i><b>Occult:</b><br /> Terrestrial Sorcery is not all bad and an allied sorcerer could bring in some handy utility spells. Otherwise, DB spirit fighting is not bad.</i><br /> Terrestrial Circle Sorcery<br /> Elemental Internalization Technique<br /> Spirit-Detecting Mirror<br /> Harmonious Wind-Luring Song<br /> Spirit-Grounding Shout<br /> Spirit-Shredding Attack<br /> <br /> <i><b>Performance:</b><br /> These vary a lot in utility, but Soul-Stirring Performance Method is probably the strongest DB UMI effect. Several serve double-duty to enhance musical fighting techniques from Three-String Sword Prana and Vibrating Strings Defence.</i><br /> Soul-Stirring Performance Method<br /> Protective Performance<br /> Talented Improvisation<br /> Invisible Street Performer Method<br /> Vibrating Strings Defence<br /> Tireless String-Plucking Meditation<br /> Three-String Sword Prana<br /> <br /> <b><i>Presence:</i></b><br /> <i>A mix of low key social effects, defences and willpower-sapping combat taunts. Not bad, worth at least a dip for the first three.</i><br /> Auspicious First Meeting<br /> Glowing Coal Radiance<br /> Aura of Invulnerability<br /> Terrifying (Element) Dragon Roar<br /> Unbearable Taunt Technique<br /> Moth to Candle<br /> Warlord's Convocation<br /> <br /> <i><b>Resistance:</b><br /> Strength of Stones is great for boosting the groups's stats. Mountain Toppling Method is usually only good in conjunction with an extra-action Charm using a jade weapon.</i><br /> Ox-Body Technique<br /> Strength of Stones Technique<br /> Impervious Skin of Stone Meditation<br /> (Element) Protection Form (Wood, Air)<br /> Mountain Toppling Method<br /> <br /> <i><b>Ride:</b><br /> Not a lot to offer here unless you want to get into mass combat, and I don't. </i><br /> Heaven Graced Riding Technique <br /> Ebony Spur Technique<br /> Great Heart Companion<br /> Elemental Halo's Mercy<br /> <br /> <i><b>Sail:</b><br /> If you reeeeally want a grizzled sea captain go all in and get everything for Waves Like Clouds Voyage. Otherwise skip it.</i><br /> <br /> <b><i>Socialize:</i></b><br /> <i>Generally very weak, but it fits the Cheerful Carouser concept too well to pass up. Have your party Charms.</i><br /> Sweeten-the-Tap Method<br /> Auspicious Merrymaking Technique<br /> Wary Yellow Dog Attitude<br /> Blood Cries for Blood<br /> Warm-Faced Seduction Style<br /> Smoothing Over the Past Technique<br /> Brother Against Brother Insinuation<br /> <br /> <i><b>Stealth:</b></i><br /> <i>Generally pretty good at assisting any group covert action.</i><br /> Distracting Breeze Meditation<br /> Deadly Mirage Ambush<br /> Trackless Passage Style<br /> Wind Walking Technique<br /> Feeling the Air Technique<br /> Soundless Action Prana<br /> Zone of Silence Stance<br /> Dragon Shroud Technique<br /> Hidden Maelstrom Cloak<br /> <br /> <b><i>Survival:</i></b><br /> <i>It's not very good. This one is good for tracking but I would skip the rest.</i><br /> Quarry Revelation Technique<br /> <br /> <i><b>Thrown:</b></i><br /> <i>Good mix of attacks and defences. Elemental Armor is one of the best DB defence Charms. Attacks mix well with Elemental Bolt.</i><br /> Loyal Weapon<br /> Persistent Hornet Attack<br /> Deadly Blades of the Five Dragons<br /> Whirlwind Shield Form<br /> Vengeful Gust Counterattack<br /> Elemental Armor Technique<br /> Hurricane Hand Gesture<br /> <br /> <i><b>War:</b><br /> If you use Mass Combat a lot, War is hands down the best DB tree. Even if you don't, Ramparts of Obedient Earth and Dragon Vortex are definitely worth getting.</i><br /> Enfolded in the Dragon's Wings<br /> Phantom Warrior Horde<br /> Blazing Courageous Swordsman Inspiration<br /> Ramparts of Obedient Earth<br /> Dragon Seared Battlefield<br /> Dragon Vortex Attack<br /> Wrath Directing Gesture (Follow, Sculpt, Shield)<br /> <br /> Phew, that ended up a lot longer than I thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T08:00:21-07:00","id":674211,"title":"","content":"Given the concept I might look into Crane Style or Dreaming Pearl Courtesan (plague did an excellent rewrite of the latter).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T08:08:45-07:00","id":674214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/673934-making-a-legendary-first-age-dragonblood?p=674211#post674211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given the concept I might look into Crane Style or Dreaming Pearl Courtesan (plague did an excellent rewrite of the latter).</div> </div> </div> </div>Crane is a great choice. Group defence Charms (With one Mind and Virtuous Negation Defence) effectively allow the character to counterattack on behalf of the entire group. Empowering Justice Redirection boosts accuracy beyond the normal DB limits; invaluable as they lack perfect attacks and DV halvers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T08:12:34-07:00","id":674217,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I felt like it was aesthetically appropriate. Not to mention that Crane is also one of the few CMA with a full Chungian defense suite, which DBs would want in a Usurpation game. I feel like it combines well with Snake as well if you want to know multiple MA.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T08:30:41-07:00","id":674227,"title":"","content":"Crumplepunch, what - the - hell?<br /> Investigation <i>weak</i>? Have you never seen a DB ask the same question 10 times in a row to strip a character of all their willpower, or get a perfect lie detection? Have you not seen the aggressive power of Revelation of Associate's Hunch, a charm which at one point I think 2/3rds of our PCs have, and caused the ST to have to write lists of associates for every NPC because he knew we'd use it whenever they met us?<br /> The 2.5 errata downpowered it a bit, but did also make it a pretty good Celestial detector.<br /> <br /> (Please note: my shock is just for effect. I'm not trying to be aggressive.)<i>\u200b</i><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T10:29:53-07:00","id":674373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/673934-making-a-legendary-first-age-dragonblood?p=674227#post674227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Crumplepunch, what - the - hell?<br /> Investigation <i>weak</i>? Have you never seen a DB ask the same question 10 times in a row to strip a character of all their willpower, or get a perfect lie detection? Have you not seen the aggressive power of Revelation of Associate's Hunch, a charm which at one point I think 2/3rds of our PCs have, and caused the ST to have to write lists of associates for every NPC because he knew we'd use it whenever they met us?<br /> The 2.5 errata downpowered it a bit, but did also make it a pretty good Celestial detector.<br /> <br /> (Please note: my shock is just for effect. I'm not trying to be aggressive.)<i>\u200b</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, let's take a closer look at it.<br /> <br /> <b>Scent-of-Crime Method</b> - Lets you detect how guilty someone is feeling. This doesn't necessarily provide any helpful information (it doesn't necessarily tell you what they are feeling guilty about and some people feel no guilt) so I am pretty ambivalent about it. However, it is cheap and scene-long, so you can pick guilty-feeling people out of a crowd. It's ok.<br /> <br /> <b>Falsehood Unearthing Attitude </b>- A poor substitute for Judge's Ear, it fails against evasions and half-truths. It is useful for interrogating people, but it can be difficult to use subtly or casually. While you <i>can</i> repeatedly ask the same question ten times, unless your storyteller is telling you that they are lying and spending willpower to avoid it, I'm not sure why you would, and doing that undermines the intended weakness of the Charm.<br /> <br /> <b>Tampering Detection Technique </b>- Examine an object, reveals any tampering throughout the last year. This may provide some use but is generally unimpressive.<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodhound's Nose Technique </b>- An interesting idea that is limited by the practicalities of the game. When invited to give players open-ended clues to the identity of the perpetrator, the storyteller is probably going to give the clues that he intended the party investigator to uncover anyway. Being able to Sherlock-scan a crime scene is nice, though.<br /> <br /> <b>Clear Water Prana </b>- For the princely sum of 5m, 1wp, Clear Water Prana detects concealed objects within Essence yards, except when they are concealed with Celestial Charms or Sorcery. I am struggling to think of a possible use for this Charm. When would you activate it? If you have reason to suspect something is (mundanely) concealed nearby, under what circumstances would a regular Investigation roll not suffice?<br /> <br /> <b>Revelation of Associates Hunch</b> - Aside from being an absolute pain for the Storyteller, this isn't bad for information gathering. However, it does have the ignominious distinction of being the only Charm to have the risible Celestial-No restriction <i>added</i> in errata.<br /> <br /> <b>Homeward Trail Discovery Method </b>- Potentially useable, but I think with Investigation 4+ and knowing a list of closest friends, family and associates, the investigator would be able to narrow down his target's home anyway.<br /> <br /> <b>Dredged Murmurs Hunch </b>- This is a plot level investigation power that puts the Sidereal google spider to shame. I didn't recommend it above because it's something that should really only be in the hands of PCs.<br /> <br /> Overall it's not <i>bad </i>(except for Clear Water Prana) but I feel justified in saying it's one of the weaker trees.<br /> <br /> It can certainly do things other Charms cannot, but Charm purchases have a tight opportunity cost and how much use you will get out of an Investigation investment needs to be compared against investments in other areas. Compared with the breadth of utility you can get out of the Bureaucracy deal making Charms or the Linguistics communication tree, Investigation falls short. <br /> <br /> Dredged Murmurs Hunch is the exception, but you need to buy almost all the other Charms to access it.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":2093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","user":"Crumplepunch","date":". 09-22-2015, 01:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T11:17:44-07:00","id":674409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/673934-making-a-legendary-first-age-dragonblood?p=674373#post674373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Dredged Murmurs Hunch </b>- This is a plot level investigation power that puts the Sidereal google spider to shame. I didn't recommend it above because it's something that should really only be in the hands of PCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>But the OP is making a PC... did you mean only NPCs?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T11:26:01-07:00","id":674415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/673934-making-a-legendary-first-age-dragonblood?p=674409#post674409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the OP is making a PC... did you mean only NPCs?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooooh, I misread and thought that OP was making an ally for his Solar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T00:56:55-07:00","id":675014,"title":"","content":"Thanks for all the replies! So far they've been extremely helpful!<br /> <br /> <br /> Got two more questions, and they're kind of doozies.<br /> <br /> The first is what artifacts would you recommend I get, socially and physically based?<br /> <br /> <br /> And attached to the first in a way, what Martial Arts Styles do you recommend?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Keep in mind, my ST is house-ruling lots of stuff, one of which is that he will make it possible, through extreme effort, for a Dragonblood to learn SMA.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Further house-rules and build notable stuff: It's the Legendary Dragonblood char gen, after that it is 500XP, and we can buy Abilities past 3 without spending BP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3052,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3052-blackshade10","user":"blackshade10","date":". 09-23-2015, 04:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3052-blackshade10","name":"blackshade10","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T02:57:20-07:00","id":675081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackshade10</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/673934-making-a-legendary-first-age-dragonblood?p=675014#post675014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for all the replies! So far they've been extremely helpful!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Further house-rules and build notable stuff: It's the Legendary Dragonblood char gen, after that it is 500XP, and we can buy Abilities past 3 without spending BP.</div> </div> </div> </div>Holy mother of god that's a lot of XP on top of legendary chargen. Especially considering how small some of the DB charm trees are. With that much XP and with such a hi start point already you're going to be either really diverse in native charms sor going pretty hard into MA. Are the immaculate styles a thing yet in your game? If you're a fire aspect or have used DB medicine to take the fire aspect anima power the capstone for Fire Dragon is amazing. Pair that up with the capstones for air and earth dragon and you're getting a pretty damn powerful attack if you can set it up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T03:12:15-07:00","id":675086,"title":"","content":"With that much XP, no reason not to be a Sorcerer. Grab a couple independence spells like Demon of the First Circle, Cirrus Skiff, and stuff like that. The goal would be that you can go to ground at any point, and need only your Sorcery to survive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T03:47:06-07:00","id":675101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackshade10</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/673934-making-a-legendary-first-age-dragonblood?p=675014#post675014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Further house-rules and build notable stuff: It's the Legendary Dragonblood char gen, after that it is 500XP, and we can buy Abilities past 3 without spending BP.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you can get Essence 6, take Mantle of Elemental Fusion and Ordained Talon of Draconic Fury.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1628-emeraldstreak","name":"emeraldstreak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1628_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T10:41:29-07:00","id":675394,"title":"","content":"For Martial Arts, Earth Dragon is worth it for the capstone alone. It has many effects, all of them excellent, including a Crippling defence DBs otherwise lack. As mentioned above, Crane is also a very good choice.<br /> <br /> I have a couple of docs of custom <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1TMcVNd0NGNm_2x_avBHfRkk-X3mmoFpN8PbSqoKXqMY/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\">Charms </a>that you might make some use of. I developed them in a game where I play a DB alongside a Celestial group and I seem to be able to keep pace. A few of them do rely on house rules peculiar to that game so use your discretion. In particular I revised a few War Charms to keep them useful in a game that steers clear of Mass Combat.<br /> <br /> I tend to find going artifact light is the best approach, especially if you have Charms like Perfection of the Earth Body that give you artifact-scale weapons naturally. Those commitment motes eat into your precious mote pool. Hearthstone Bracers are always a solid option though, the dodge boost and Speed reduction are invaluable.<br /> <br /> Oh, and don't forget Eric Minton's DB hearthstone Charms <a href=\"https://ericminton.wordpress.com/2014/08/13/ink-monkey-bones-14-essence-lensing-jewel/\" target=\"_blank\">here </a>and <a href=\"https://ericminton.wordpress.com/2014/05/21/ink-monkey-bones-2-hearthstone-weaponry/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.<br /> <br /> Hearthstone selection is tricky because there is a terribly fine grey space between the three axes of dull, broken and useless. For a social boost, the Jewel of Lawgiver's Authority is pretty nice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":2093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","user":"Crumplepunch","date":". 09-23-2015, 01:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T11:53:07-07:00","id":675566,"title":"","content":"the dragon styles really should not be available in the first age","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T12:49:47-07:00","id":675615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/673934-making-a-legendary-first-age-dragonblood?p=675566#post675566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the dragon styles really should not be available in the first age</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe they were developed in preparation for the Usurpation, which is what OP is playing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T13:02:49-07:00","id":675634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/673934-making-a-legendary-first-age-dragonblood?p=675615#post675615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I believe they were developed in preparation for the Usurpation, which is what OP is playing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fairly sure they don't predate the Usurpation and were developed during the Shogunate era along with the Immaculate texts themselves. Could be wrong but this is how I thought it went.<br /> <br /> Hiding the conspiracy was hard enough without adding &quot;here are these 5 MAs that work ESPECIALLY well for DBs and wow our dojos sure are overflowing with students&quot; to the mix.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 09-23-2015, 04:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T13:10:17-07:00","id":675655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/673934-making-a-legendary-first-age-dragonblood?p=675634#post675634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fairly sure they don't predate the Usurpation and were developed during the Shogunate era along with the Immaculate texts themselves. Could be wrong but this is how I thought it went.<br /> <br /> Hiding the conspiracy was hard enough without adding &amp;quot;here are these 5 MAs that work ESPECIALLY well for DBs and wow our dojos sure are overflowing with students&amp;quot; to the mix.</div> </div> </div> </div>Either way, this particular campaign might have them developed early. The elemental MA dojos could easily be described to a solar as making their DB monks even more powerful to get a leg up over the competition or something. Remember, one of the reasons the usurpation worked was because the Solars were too trusting/arrogant to believe that their servants were even capable of rebellion. Especially since so few DBs can learn CMA anyway,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T13:52:23-07:00","id":675686,"title":"","content":"They were developed as part of the Immaculate Order.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T14:11:23-07:00","id":675691,"title":"","content":"It is not <i>inconceivable</i> that, in the First Age, there were a collection of Celestial Martial Arts dedicated to emulating the Elemental Dragons that allowed the Dragon Blooded host to attune themselves to multiple elements in the pursuit of Enlightenment. Mechanically there is zero reason not to just port the mechanics for the Immaculate Dragon Styles if someone wants to use those hypothetical First Age styles. The special combat boosts that Dragon Blooded get for knowing the styles should probably be dropped and in the unlikely event that a modern dragon blooded learns these old styles and the modern styles they should be seen as different styles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T23:52:41-07:00","id":676111,"title":"","content":"Our characters ALL have a destiny of playing a key role in the Usurpation in some way, among the most important figures in it, hence why the GM has decided to give us ultra-high power because at the end of the day, our enemy is going to be a ton of Elder Solars. Our own master went from &quot;egotistical occasional jackass but OK&quot; to &quot;megalomaniac sadistic god-complex&quot; and we have to escape from him at the start of the game.<br /> <br /> So largely what I'm hearing is Dragon Styles are fairly boss, Namely Fire, Earth, and Air? I remembering hearing that Wood is a trap(because of the Form Weapon), unsure on Water. Depending on certain things, my GM is very open to house-ruling stuff.<br /> <br /> <br /> And while they may not have existed by the book yet, it's possible that one of the PC's ends up inventing it. Our characters are supposed to be quite important, hell, mine has Destiny 5.<br /> <br /> <br /> And Artifact light, but definitely should get Ordained Talon of Draconic Fury...<br /> <br /> Gonna go read those custom charms now!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Side question: Opinion on 2.5 Violet Bier of Sorrows + Rings of Saturn(Glories book)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3052,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3052-blackshade10","user":"blackshade10","date":". 09-24-2015, 03:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3052-blackshade10","name":"blackshade10","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T01:56:50-07:00","id":676201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackshade10</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/673934-making-a-legendary-first-age-dragonblood?p=676111#post676111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Our characters ALL have a destiny of playing a key role in the Usurpation in some way, among the most important figures in it, hence why the GM has decided to give us ultra-high power because at the end of the day, our enemy is going to be a ton of Elder Solars. Our own master went from &amp;quot;egotistical occasional jackass but OK&amp;quot; to &amp;quot;megalomaniac sadistic god-complex&amp;quot; and we have to escape from him at the start of the game.<br /> <br /> So largely what I'm hearing is Dragon Styles are fairly boss, Namely Fire, Earth, and Air? I remembering hearing that Wood is a trap(because of the Form Weapon), unsure on Water. Depending on certain things, my GM is very open to house-ruling stuff.<br /> <br /> <br /> And while they may not have existed by the book yet, it's possible that one of the PC's ends up inventing it. Our characters are supposed to be quite important, hell, mine has Destiny 5.<br /> <br /> <br /> And Artifact light, but definitely should get Ordained Talon of Draconic Fury...<br /> <br /> Gonna go read those custom charms now!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Side question: Opinion on 2.5 Violet Bier of Sorrows + Rings of Saturn(Glories book)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I've always liked VBoS, and if you're going to be learning from a sidereal master it makes a lot of sense and would be a good choice.<br /> <br /> Also if you're going for an immaculate grandmaster style character who's mastered all the dragon styles you won't be using form weapons. Instead you'll use earth dragon to make your fists like unto goremauls except faster and more accurate, fire dragon to ignite them blazing hot and air dragon to extend their reach out over a dozen yards. What wood dragon will let you do is heal wounds instantly, and even heal the wounds of others, and water dragon has a perfect defence and ways of stealing your opponents essence and stuff. Really they're all good.<br /> <br /> Normally I would never suggest taking all five, but you actually can with your super chargen, and they cover a lot of ground. Stealth is in air and earth, presence is in wood and fire, resistance is in wood and earth, dodge is in air and fire, athletics and awareness charms are also in air, survival in wood, and they've all got a bit of occult.<br /> <br /> On the other hand it's a massive investment, you might be better off with VBoS and RoS.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T02:03:47-07:00","id":676204,"title":"","content":"The Rings of Saturn get most of their bonuses against people who are weaker than you which seems ill-fitting for this situation (are you expecting FA Solars to be a lower essence rating than you?) Violet Bier of Sorrows is still kind of crazy though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T02:31:37-07:00","id":676219,"title":"","content":"Good point on the Rings of Saturn bit...<br /> <br /> <br /> I won't lie, it's REALLY tempting to go the whole Grandmaster route with the character, and with the starting XP I could get all of them, but I think that I want to start with no more than 2, tops. Partly because I want to get used to the charms and learn the Styles myself well before I go getting them all.<br /> <br /> The character would learn the Martial Arts only with the permission of the Solar Master, likely to be his champion in tournaments. Flashy and effective in tournament combat. Do any of the Styles lean toward that style of fighting in particular?<br /> <br /> Alternatively, do you have a recommendation on which Style would be most helpful? I've been looking at the Charm that grants me Form weapons as well, in case I could use it for Ordained Talon of Draconic Fury. <br /> <br /> <br /> And yet another question, reading over the Enlightenment Charms, any preference/advised? I'm leaning toward Tiger-and-Bear, since those are First Age methods, and would make sense. Others are still possible, but my PC or another would have to develop them.<br /> <br /> And yet ANOTHER question(I'm on a roll): Should any Terrestrial Martial Arts be considered? I've been eyeing Ivory Pestle Style, Swaying Grass(The PC is a dancer), and Even Blade. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3052,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3052-blackshade10","user":"blackshade10","date":". 09-24-2015, 05:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3052-blackshade10","name":"blackshade10","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T06:56:22-07:00","id":676355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackshade10</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/673934-making-a-legendary-first-age-dragonblood?p=676111#post676111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So largely what I'm hearing is Dragon Styles are fairly boss, Namely Fire, Earth, and Air? I remembering hearing that Wood is a trap(because of the Form Weapon), unsure on Water. Depending on certain things, my GM is very open to house-ruling stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Water is probably the strongest overall. Water and Air have the best Form Charms because they add to MA attacks and DVs, effectively giving Dragon-Bloods an equivalent of Infinite Ability Mastery that they otherwise lack. Earth is very strong for Perfection of the Earth Body and Weapon Breaking Defence Technique, both incredibly powerful Charms.<br /> <br /> Wood is complicated. It is awkwardly designed and many of its Charms are poorly written and difficult to use. However, it is excellent at one thing: healing. Its form gives you passive regeneration and it also has a Charm that lets you absorb damage from your allies. In personal combat it is a weak style, but in its group support niche it is definitely worth having. It also combines very well with Dragon-Blooded Medicine. DB Medicine can covert Aggravated to Lethal and Lethal to Bashing, while Wood Dragon can heal Lethal quickly and Bashing even more quickly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackshade10</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/673934-making-a-legendary-first-age-dragonblood?p=676219#post676219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yet ANOTHER question(I'm on a roll): Should any Terrestrial Martial Arts be considered? I've been eyeing Ivory Pestle Style, Swaying Grass(The PC is a dancer), and Even Blade.</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally, TMAs are underpowered and overpriced compared to native DB Charms. The sadly backwards truth is that lacking a version of Swallowing the Lotus Root, DBs have little incentive to invest in them. <br /> <br /> Swaying Grass is okay, it has a couple of Charms that can help out a high Performance fighter. <br /> <br /> Dean Shomshak, the writer of Ivory Pestle, made some patches to the style that can be found <a href=\"https://exalted-silver-trout.obsidianportal.com/wikis/ivory-pestle-style-patches\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.<br /> <br /> Even Blade is... varied. Some of its Charms are definitely not 2.5 friendly, notably Gruesome Wood King Revelry. Some of its variant Charms would embarrass CMA balance. I would avoid it or try to find a good rewrite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":2093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","user":"Crumplepunch","date":". 09-24-2015, 10:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T07:37:05-07:00","id":676373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackshade10</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/673934-making-a-legendary-first-age-dragonblood?p=676219#post676219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I've been looking at the Charm that grants me Form weapons as well, in case I could use it for Ordained Talon of Draconic Fury.<br /> <br /> And yet ANOTHER question(I'm on a roll): Should any Terrestrial Martial Arts be considered? I've been eyeing Ivory Pestle Style, Swaying Grass(The PC is a dancer), and Even Blade.</div> </div> </div> </div>Look up the NPC writeups at the end of Dreams - the elderly Dragon-Blooded has a Charm that can add weapons to Styles. Also, shields used to be armor in 2.0, but in 2.5 they are weapons, so nearly all armored Martial Arts lost their benefits.<br /> <br /> There are Terrestrial Martial Arts that can be considered, but the correct way to build a character begins at figuring out what do you want him to do, then how he does it in general, and only then the particular Charms, gear, etc. For instance, Ivory Pestle has a good flurry charm, and a Form that can deal with penalties to DV. So even Celestials looking for these two things can benefit from taking it. But other approaches to the character will look for different things, ie Swaying Grass has a movement flurrybreaker and can shore up Air Dragon's Sight (but DBs have better options for both in their charmset, unlike some Celestials), Terrestrial Hero boosts clinches, Five-Dragon can ignore hardness and inflict aggravated, Jade Mountain can reduce post-soak damage, Falling Blossom has a perfect attack, Night Breeze doubles onslaught penalties, White Veil, if it existed, could poison without damage, Crimson Pentacle can resolve your actions prior to anyone else's, Even Blade has surprise attack and mote regenerator off damage, Fivefold Shadow can guarantee acting on tick 0, Arbiter can grant extra Willpower and boosts stunt awards, Golden Exhalation has the lowest rung of DV-propping counterattack, etc.<br /> <br /> The above are building blocks, or answers, but to use them best you need to ask the right questions first, ie &quot;do I need a flurry charm in high XP First Age game? Is my native charmset good enough, or should I look for other options like Ivory Pestle or Arms of the Unconquered Sun?&quot;, or &quot;do I have a viable tick-long perfect? And if not what flurrybreakers are available to me? do i want to risk a movement-based flurrybreaker in a high XP game or should I stick to an absolute one like Day&amp;Night Kata or Dawn's Parable Defense (the latter of course is for Solars only)?&quot;, or &quot;do I want a defense against Crippling in 2.5? Do I have a decent one in my native charmset (decent = reasonably successful, cheap, and XP-intensive), or should I look into other options like Arms of the Unconquered Sun or the Infernal 4-dot hearthstone?&quot;, or &quot;will I be spending XP for Posion defense, or spending Background for Stone of Earth's Blood and antivenin?&quot;<br /> <br /> Keep in mind many of these &quot;if's&quot; depend on the style of your ST. Say, it is a fairly certain bet your character needs a defense against surprise attacks, preferably scene-long; but it is impossible to tell how much your character will benefit from an ability to launch surprise attacks - that entirely depends on the ST's design of opponents.<br /> <br /> PS. If you use Merits, be sure to take Extra Favored Ability x2 in addition to the usual ones. Likewise, if you use Kata Bracers get them for a martial artist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1628-emeraldstreak","name":"emeraldstreak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1628_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T07:46:58-07:00","id":676378,"title":"","content":"All the Dragon Styles and VBoS got errata'd, so if you're playing in 2.5 they should be fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T09:00:55-07:00","id":676432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackshade10</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/673934-making-a-legendary-first-age-dragonblood?p=676219#post676219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yet another question, reading over the Enlightenment Charms, any preference/advised? I'm leaning toward Tiger-and-Bear, since those are First Age methods, and would make sense. Others are still possible, but my PC or another would have to develop them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Iris Bulb Discourse already existed in the First Age. The Immaculate initiation is the one that hadn't been invented yet.<br /> <br /> According to the 1E Player's Guide, there are tales of a First Age option to spend mere months (instead of years) with ALL of your essence committed to an esoteric magical material sculpture that initiates your soul, but it would be up to your ST to decide if the sculpture method teaches you any charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}